Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 04/28/2023]
1. Unless noted, resonance strengths from Endt 1990, 1998, which incorporates Berg et al. 1977, Keinonen et al. 1977, Goerres et al. 1982, Goerres et al. 1983,
   and Becker et al. 1992.
2. Er = 96 keV: used same information as in Tab. 10 of Iliadis et al. 2001: an upper limit of C2S < 0.02 was derived from Fig. 1 and Tab. I in the 21Ne(d,p)
   work of Neogy et al. 1972, assuming the level corresponds to the 0+ mirror at 6235 keV in 22Ne (Endt 1998). This is also the procedure applied first by
   El Eid & Champagne 1995. Gp upper limit is recalculated using new Er value.
3. Er = 18 keV: Jp=2+ assumed (s-wave resonance) for upper limit estimate. Gp upper limit is recalculated using new Er value.
4. DC was recalculated using experimental C2S values listed in Endt 1977 and Garrett et al. 1971. Because the C2S values mostly rest on a single experiment,
   we will assume a DC S factor uncertainty of 50%.
5. For broad resonances between Er = 670 and 1937 keV: Gp and Gg calculated from wg and G given in Endt 1990, assuming G = Gp and Gg = wg/w.
6. Subthreshold resonances will likely not impact the total S factor, based on tests using measured C2S values from Garret et al. 1971.


